  "caption": "Quinn decided the safest plan for rheumatoid arthritis was to rest all month. By week three, the stairs felt taller and Quinn felt weaker.\n\nRA is an immune condition, not wear and tear. Supervised exercise is generally safe and helpful, while staying inactive can cost muscle, fitness and heart health.\n\nWhat often helps: combine aerobic and strength exercise, lower the intensity during flares rather than stopping, build a hand plan with your therapist, use easy-grip tools, and keep up your rheumatology reviews.\n\nGet checked if small joints swell for around six weeks, morning stiffness lasts over an hour, or you notice fever, weight loss, or neck pain with hand numbness.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
